text The hallway, illuminated by fluorescent lamps, is filled with a heavy atmosphere.
text The doctor had told Sanae-san he'd done everything he could do.
text ...and that the rest would be up to his own life force.
text The old man... he'd saved many people's lives.
text And probably... also that young man's mind.
text Still...
text I look at Sanae-san's profile as she continues to wait with a smile, praying.
text He was someone who'd always go off somewhere...
text Someone who always did reckless things...
text I can't help but feel sorry for her, since she can't do anything but continue on waiting...
text That's something I've always thought to myself.
text The old man is a wonderful human being.
text But I wonder if he's also a wonderful husband.
text Just what is Sanae-san to him...?
text Is she the same as all those other people?
text I can't help but feel that way.
text Is there even a single thing that he can vow for Sanae-san, and not someone else?
